! maintenance_bits_store.strap -- WORD 4, THE MAINTENANCE BITS: OUTSIDE
! MAINTENANCE MODE ANY STORE LEAVES IT 0.  Ones are stored into word 4
! by five paths, and every read-back is zero.
!
! THE RULE, read from the page images (2026-11-19):
!   * Reference Manual printed p.35 (PDF p.38), "Maintenance Bits": "The
!     64 bits of storage location 4 are reserved for maintenance
!     purposes.  These bits are active only when the machine is in the
!     maintenance mode.  When it is not in this mode, they act like the
!     bits of location 0.  After an initial program load, this location
!     contains the first word read from the input unit.  This is the
!     control word for the initial load.  Any store to location 4 causes
!     it to contain a 0 with correct check bits."
!   * C22-6578 Appendix A3, "7030 SPECIAL REGISTERS" (PDF p.56): "$MB
!     (MAINTENANCE BITS WHEN MACHINE IS IN MAINTENANCE MODE.  ALSO
!     INITIAL CONTROL WORD FOR IPL.  OTHERWISE BEHAVES LIKE $Z)", kind
!     "MEMORY / MANUAL KEYS".
!   * pocket card X22-6533-1 (docs/pcard-1.png): "4  Maintenance Bits
!     64  0-63" -- the width in maintenance mode, not a contradiction.
!   The model has no maintenance mode, so outside it is the only mode.
!   The IPL's own store into word 4 is the exchange's, not a program
!   store, and keeps its word (StretchStorage.bsv loadWord4; pinned by
!   the IPL test's W4 check in tests/run_tests.sh).
!
! Word 4 is not in the protected area (the pocket card gives it no P).
!
! FIVE STORE PATHS, each read back by an instruction into ordinary
! storage, not only by the testbench's look at word 4:
!   1. ST(BU,64,8),W4 of 64 ones -- the whole word.  Read back at once
!      (RB1) and again after two NOPs (RB2).
!   2. SV,$X1,W4, value all ones -- STORE VALUE, bits 0-24 (RB3).
!   3. SX,$X2,W4 of an index word of all ones -- STORE INDEX, 64 bits
!      (RB4).
!   4. TI,1,ONES,W4 -- TRANSMIT, one word, the core's rl_xmit path
!      rather than an execute arm (RB5).
!   5. ST(BU,8),W4+.32 of a byte of ones -- a VFL field of 8 bits in the
!      middle of the word.  "Any store" means the whole word becomes 0,
!      not just the field (RB6).
!   Expected of each: 0.  W4 itself is 0 at the halt.
!
! The read-back words start as (16)5555555555555555, so a read-back that
! never happened cannot pass as a 0.
!
! RESULT, 2026-11-19: PASS on the fixed model (StretchStorage.bsv's
! addrMaintenanceBits arm pulses w4StoreW; commitWord4 writes 0): RB1-RB6
! and W4 all 0, PC 4265.
!
! PROVEN DISCRIMINATING, OBSERVED (a scratch copy of the tree):
!   INJECTION = THE STORE KEPT, as before 2026-11-19 (the arm made
!     "addrMaintenanceBits: w4LoadW.wset(v);", i.e. the old
!     "maintenanceBits <= v" through the one committing rule)
!     -> FAIL on 7 pins: RB1-RB6 and W4 all 0xffffffffffffffff (RB6 too:
!     the 8-bit field merged into the ones TI left).  PC 4265 passes.
!   The same injection leaves decks/other_cpu_width.strap and the IPL
!   test passing.  Reverted by the inverse substitution; cmp identical to
!   the working file.
!
W4      SYN, 4.0                     ! word 4, the maintenance bits ($MB)
        SLC, (8)4100.0
START   BD,  $+.32
        L(BU,64,8), ONES             ! accumulator := 64 ones
        ST(BU,64,8), W4              ! 1. all of word 4
        L(BU,64,8), W4               !    read back at once
        ST(BU,64,8), RB1
        NOP
        NOP
        L(BU,64,8), W4               !    and again, later
        ST(BU,64,8), RB2
        LV,  $X1, ONES               ! value field all ones
        SV,  $X1, W4                 ! 2. STORE VALUE: bits 0-24
        L(BU,64,8), W4
        ST(BU,64,8), RB3
        LX,  $X2, ONES               ! index word all ones
        SX,  $X2, W4                 ! 3. STORE INDEX: all 64 bits
        L(BU,64,8), W4
        ST(BU,64,8), RB4
        TI,  1, ONES, W4             ! 4. TRANSMIT one word
        L(BU,64,8), W4
        ST(BU,64,8), RB5
        L(BU,64,8), ONES
        ST(BU,8), W4+.32             ! 5. an 8-bit field at 4.32
        L(BU,64,8), W4
        ST(BU,64,8), RB6
PASS    BEW, $
        SLC, (8)6000.0
ONES    DD(BU,64), (16)FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF
RB1     DD(BU,64), (16)5555555555555555
RB2     DD(BU,64), (16)5555555555555555
RB3     DD(BU,64), (16)5555555555555555
RB4     DD(BU,64), (16)5555555555555555
RB5     DD(BU,64), (16)5555555555555555
RB6     DD(BU,64), (16)5555555555555555
        END, START
